    "Reduce forecast overshoots following strong upward sentiment spikes (sentiment > 0.20) by 10-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Adjust downward forecasts when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0.00) by adding a 5-10% bias correction to reflect bearish momentum.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates > 10% from recent 5-day average, adjust toward historical mean.",
    "For long-term horizon (30d) forecasts, reduce volatility by smoothing out extreme outliers using a 3-point moving average filter.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00), prioritize alignment with recent 15-day price trend rather than model extrapolation.",
    "Correct for lagged reactions: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, delay correction by 1-2 days to account for market inertia."
  ]
